From b5bd5798383ff842048d3f5af9e7ebf2a79030e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KhaiWenTan <khai.wen.tan@intel.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 21:52:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] net: stmmac: skip PHY device check for fixed link mode

In fixed link mode, there will be no PHY device setup. Therefore,
adding stmmac_get_phydev() into the stmmac_dvr_probe() will only
return error and halt the setup process for fixed phy.

Before calling stmmac_get_phydev(), check if the priv->plat->phy_addr
is having a valid value. If valid, we may continue calling the
function. If not, skip the function since there will be no PHY device.

By checking the priv->plat->phy_addr before the function, fixed link
mode will be able to finish the setup in stmmac_drv_probe().

Fixes: 14e35c66b1db ("net: stmmac: Set mac_managed_pm flag from stmmac to resolve race condition")
Signed-off-by: KhaiWenTan <khai.wen.tan@intel.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index da19352396ad2..35d61e9f29c6f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -7846,10 +7846,15 @@ int stmmac_dvr_probe(struct device *device,
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_pcs_setup;
 
-	ret = stmmac_get_phydev(priv, &phydev);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
-	phydev->mac_managed_pm = true;
+	/* Only look up the PHY by MDIO address when phy_addr is known
+	 * (e.g. fixed-link keeps it unset).
+	 */
+	if (priv->plat->phy_addr >= 0) {
+		ret = stmmac_get_phydev(priv, &phydev);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		phydev->mac_managed_pm = true;
+	}
 
 	ret = stmmac_phy_setup(priv);
 	if (ret) {
-- 
2.43.0

